<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69831" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναύλοχ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>affording a safe
			anchorage,</i> epith. of a harbour, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμένες δ᾽ ἔνι ν. αὐτῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.846
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ἐς λιμένα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					10.141
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. λιπὼν ἕδρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					460
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ ν. καὶ πετραῖα θερμὰ
			λουτρά</span> ye hot springs <i>by the haven</i> and from the
			rock (unless <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναύλοχα</span> is
			Subst.), <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				633
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχαιῶν ναύλοχοι περιπτυχαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					1015
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναυλοχώτατος λιμήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.181
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				352
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Subst., <i>station for ships, haven,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>: also neut. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναύλοχα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.984b
				</span></i>
			; cf. supr.</div>
